1
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:07,080
[Fragments of Truth]

2
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:08,640
[Episode 11]

3
00:01:12,510 --> 00:01:13,120
That's dog meat.

4
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:14,840
Some of it's gone bad.

5
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:16,430
Some parts are missing.

6
00:01:16,790 --> 00:01:17,680
Guess someone ate them.

7
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:18,710
Ouch.

8
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:22,310
What a terrible thing.

9
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:24,710
Ouch.

10
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:28,710
Who'd do something so awful?

11
00:01:28,710 --> 00:01:33,710
They even ransacked my home!

12
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:34,510
Ma'am.

13
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:35,920
Calm down.

14
00:01:36,310 --> 00:01:39,070
How can I calm down?

15
00:01:39,310 --> 00:01:43,310
Look, they even knocked Buddha over.

16
00:01:43,870 --> 00:01:46,040
Ma'am, where did the dog meat come from?

17
00:01:49,310 --> 00:01:50,280
Bought it.

18
00:01:50,510 --> 00:01:52,870
Mrs. Song, you'd better tell the truth.

19
00:01:52,870 --> 00:01:56,310
We're here about Wu Jia's disappearance.

20
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:57,680
I can tell you.

21
00:01:58,040 --> 00:02:01,120
We now suspect Wu Jia is dead.

22
00:02:10,310 --> 00:02:11,190
Amitabha.

23
00:02:11,190 --> 00:02:12,430
Buddha, protect me.

24
00:02:12,430 --> 00:02:13,190
Amitabha.

25
00:02:13,190 --> 00:02:14,120
Buddha, protect me.

26
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:15,800
Don't come after me!

27
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:18,310
I had nothing to do with it!

28
00:02:18,310 --> 00:02:20,000
- Protect me!
- Mrs. Song! Mrs. Song!

29
00:02:20,430 --> 00:02:21,120
Calm down.

30
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:24,030
First, tell us where the meat came from.

31
00:02:24,030 --> 00:02:25,030
Then we can help you.

32
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:28,590
Well...

33
00:02:29,910 --> 00:02:32,590
There are many stray dogs nearby.

34
00:02:33,190 --> 00:02:34,520
They've even bitten people.

35
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:35,910
And, uh...

36
00:02:35,910 --> 00:02:39,870
So I got snare poles and metal skewers.

37
00:02:40,470 --> 00:02:42,310
I'd kill one if it came back.

38
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:46,840
I kept the meat for myself.

39
00:02:48,910 --> 00:02:50,520
Did you spill the blood in the hallway?

40
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:52,520
Yes.

41
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:54,520
Our building is haunted.

42
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:56,800
Dog blood wards off evil.

43
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Why are you still hiding things?

44
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:00,520
Tell us.

45
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:02,840
Why spill it where Wu Jia vanished?

46
00:03:03,630 --> 00:03:06,000
I'll tell you!
I'll tell you!

47
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:13,080
Ah! A ghost!
Ah!

48
00:03:13,430 --> 00:03:15,000
Oh, my!
Ow!

49
00:03:37,910 --> 00:03:38,710
Ah!

50
00:03:41,710 --> 00:03:45,960
That night, I saw blood by the stairs.

51
00:03:46,430 --> 00:03:48,190
Then I saw a backpack.

52
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:50,710
It had money inside.

53
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:52,910
I just couldn't resist.

54
00:03:52,910 --> 00:03:56,800
But once home, I started thinking...

55
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:59,470
maybe his little boy

56
00:03:59,630 --> 00:04:02,280
had come back to avenge his dad.

57
00:04:02,870 --> 00:04:04,870
So I sprinkled some dog blood

58
00:04:05,710 --> 00:04:08,520
so the child wouldn't haunt me.

59
00:04:08,910 --> 00:04:10,840
Where's the bag?
What was inside?

60
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:14,190
The bag... I threw it away.

61
00:04:14,630 --> 00:04:18,040
But I kept the money
and everything else.

62
00:04:18,270 --> 00:04:19,270
I'll get them now.

63
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,120
Oh, right.

64
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:29,800
I washed some of the clothes too.

65
00:04:29,870 --> 00:04:31,270
I couldn't bear to throw them out.

66
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:33,920
I'll get them for you right now.

67
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:42,830
The phone and bank card are new.

68
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:45,720
Ah.

69
00:04:46,510 --> 00:04:47,870
This pendant is unusual.

70
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:50,120
It was kept with all these things,

71
00:04:52,630 --> 00:04:53,510
so it may be significant.

72
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:54,430
Uncle He.

73
00:04:55,390 --> 00:04:57,270
I know someone I can ask about it.

74
00:04:59,630 --> 00:05:00,800
Officer.

75
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:08,390
I know.
I was wrong.

76
00:05:08,390 --> 00:05:12,120
Please, don't arrest me.

77
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:13,270
Please?

78
00:05:13,270 --> 00:05:15,310
Mrs. Song, don't worry.

79
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:17,430
If it happened just as you said,

80
00:05:17,430 --> 00:05:18,870
you had nothing to do with it.

81
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,240
You won't be penalized.

82
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:21,040
Ah.

83
00:05:21,430 --> 00:05:24,310
But you'll still need to come with us

84
00:05:24,510 --> 00:05:25,390
to give a statement.

85
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:27,390
Okay, okay.
Yes.

86
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:28,310
Captain Ren.

87
00:05:28,310 --> 00:05:29,120
Yeah?

88
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:30,870
Let's go, ma'am.

89
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:32,800
Mrs. Song.

90
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:33,800
Yes?

91
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:36,190
When did this fridge get here?

92
00:05:36,430 --> 00:05:38,510
I don't recall seeing it last time.

93
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:41,070
I picked it up the night before last.

94
00:05:41,390 --> 00:05:43,720
It took a lot of work to haul it back.

95
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:45,870
Oh.

96
00:05:47,870 --> 00:05:48,310
Let's go.

97
00:05:48,310 --> 00:05:49,120
Okay.

98
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:04,870
[One day earlier]

99
00:06:04,870 --> 00:06:07,390
Officers, have some tea.

100
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:11,120
I'm sorry.

101
00:06:11,270 --> 00:06:13,070
When I had that episode last time,

102
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:16,070
I truly couldn't remember anything.

103
00:06:16,310 --> 00:06:17,120
It's okay.

104
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:19,240
We're not here about that.

105
00:06:21,310 --> 00:06:22,120
Thank you.

106
00:06:22,870 --> 00:06:23,720
This time,

107
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:25,920
we only want some basic information.

108
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,120
You don't need to be nervous.

109
00:06:27,870 --> 00:06:29,120
If you feel unwell,

110
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:30,390
we can stop at any time.

111
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:32,480
Okay.

112
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:37,510
When did your condition start?

113
00:06:39,870 --> 00:06:41,240
Not long after I got married.

114
00:06:42,190 --> 00:06:44,270
I felt unable to control my emotions.

115
00:06:45,430 --> 00:06:46,480
Once, I fought with my mother-in-law.

116
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:47,630
It got really bad.

117
00:06:49,070 --> 00:06:49,870
I just wanted to die.

118
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:53,390
Lao Wu thought something was wrong,

119
00:06:54,310 --> 00:06:55,480
so he took me to a hospital.

120
00:06:56,270 --> 00:06:58,190
They diagnosed me with bipolar disorder

121
00:06:58,870 --> 00:06:59,720
and prescribed medication.

122
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:03,240
Have you taken it all these years?

123
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:09,120
I stopped when I became pregnant.

124
00:07:11,070 --> 00:07:12,510
How did you meet Wu Jia?

125
00:07:19,190 --> 00:07:20,510
Ma'am, what can I get you?

126
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:21,510
Weigh that piece of pork belly for me.

127
00:07:21,510 --> 00:07:22,310
This one, right?

128
00:07:22,310 --> 00:07:23,430
Sure.

129
00:07:33,830 --> 00:07:35,560
It's 17.5 yuan.
Just pay 17.

130
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:36,430
Thanks.

131
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:40,510
Come back soon.

132
00:07:44,870 --> 00:07:46,390
Well, if it isn't Pork Beauty.

133
00:07:47,070 --> 00:07:49,190
Why are you selling here now?

134
00:07:50,190 --> 00:07:51,000
Hey, gorgeous.

135
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:52,830
My boss has looked for you
several times.

136
00:07:52,830 --> 00:07:55,000
A pretty girl like you selling meat?

137
00:07:55,390 --> 00:07:57,480
It breaks my boss's heart to see it.

138
00:07:58,310 --> 00:08:00,600
Get lost, or I'll call the police.

139
00:08:00,870 --> 00:08:01,680
The police?

140
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:05,480
Want me to trash your stall today?

141
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:07,310
Even the cops can't touch me.

142
00:08:07,870 --> 00:08:08,720
Hey!

143
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:10,720
Cut the crap.

144
00:08:12,430 --> 00:08:13,240
Who are you?

145
00:08:13,870 --> 00:08:15,310
Just try laying a hand on her.

146
00:08:16,270 --> 00:08:17,680
You...
Who are you?

147
00:08:17,720 --> 00:08:20,310
Listen, I'm the only one

148
00:08:20,310 --> 00:08:21,830
who gets to bully my neighbors.

149
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:22,920
Get lost.

150
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:27,040
Lao Wu wasn't bad by nature.

151
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:30,680
He later fell in with a shady crowd.

152
00:08:32,910 --> 00:08:34,720
Plus, he served time once.

153
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:37,390
After he got out,

154
00:08:39,910 --> 00:08:41,080
he changed completely.

155
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:46,120
So you still have feelings for him,

156
00:08:46,390 --> 00:08:46,870
right?

157
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:49,480
I don't know.

158
00:08:52,120 --> 00:08:53,320
But I once did.

159
00:08:54,910 --> 00:08:56,600
Then think carefully.

160
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:59,440
What happened before he disappeared?

161
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:02,120
Who was he going to meet?

162
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:05,480
Who could be tied to his disappearance?

163
00:09:08,870 --> 00:09:09,870
I don't know.

164
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:17,440
I really can't remember anything.

165
00:09:30,510 --> 00:09:32,120
Lao Wu, where did you go?

166
00:09:38,390 --> 00:09:40,080
Where did you go?

167
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:42,870
Where on earth did you go?

168
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:49,030
Do you think Chen Yun is a suspect?

169
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:50,270
She has a strong motive.

170
00:09:51,030 --> 00:09:52,270
Based on our analysis,

171
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:54,080
Wu Jia was killed in the hallway

172
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:55,870
and dragged upstairs.

173
00:09:56,270 --> 00:09:57,790
As a woman, Chen Yun

174
00:09:57,790 --> 00:10:00,390
likely lacked the strength to do that.

175
00:10:01,790 --> 00:10:03,390
The tricky part now is

176
00:10:03,390 --> 00:10:04,720
Chen Yun's mental state.

177
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:07,120
It's hard to tell if she's truly ill

178
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:08,320
or just avoiding our questions.

179
00:10:09,390 --> 00:10:09,910
I suggest we contact

180
00:10:09,910 --> 00:10:11,790
a professional assessment center

181
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,790
and have her take the MMPI.

182
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:16,390
What's that?

183
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:18,480
A psychological test.

184
00:10:18,510 --> 00:10:20,440
It can accurately determine

185
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:21,870
whether she's truly ill

186
00:10:21,870 --> 00:10:23,270
or just putting on an act.

187
00:10:24,270 --> 00:10:24,480
Okay.

188
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:26,600
I'll have someone take her there.

189
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:29,120
We also need to search this place.

190
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:31,670
If one of those two is the killer,

191
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,480
there must be evidence here.

192
00:11:42,390 --> 00:11:43,240
Are you okay?

193
00:11:43,670 --> 00:11:44,510
I'm fine.

194
00:11:50,390 --> 00:11:53,510
After Chen Yun killed her husband

195
00:11:53,670 --> 00:11:55,630
then dragged the body into this room.

196
00:11:56,670 --> 00:11:58,080
When security called the police,

197
00:11:58,120 --> 00:11:59,790
she feared we'd trace him here,

198
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:02,670
so she rushed to hide him in the fridge.

199
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,870
But the fridge was too small

200
00:12:04,870 --> 00:12:06,510
to hold a grown man.

201
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:08,630
So she took out a cleaver

202
00:12:08,870 --> 00:12:11,670
and cut his body in two.

203
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:15,270
Then she cut up and dumped the remains.

204
00:12:15,630 --> 00:12:18,000
Even when I came here last time,

205
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,870
some remains were still in the fridge.

206
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:24,240
But forensics ran a luminol test here

207
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:26,510
and found no unusual blood residue.

208
00:12:26,670 --> 00:12:27,670
She cleaned up every trace,

209
00:12:27,840 --> 00:12:28,790
including the fridge.

210
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:30,080
She replaced it with this one,

211
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:32,120
so when I came here last time,

212
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:33,240
I wouldn't suspect anything.

213
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:35,750
So the fridge at Mrs. Song's place

214
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,270
was the one that held the body.

215
00:12:37,270 --> 00:12:38,080
Exactly.

216
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:40,670
If Hao Jun's team checks carefully,

217
00:12:40,870 --> 00:12:42,240
they'll find traces of the remains

218
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:43,630
inside that fridge.

219
00:12:45,390 --> 00:12:47,120
Expand the search for the body.

220
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:48,240
Yes.

221
00:13:28,830 --> 00:13:30,890
♪I stand in a fire-tempered jungle♪

222
00:13:30,890 --> 00:13:32,840
♪Withered leaves fall
as my strength runs dry♪

223
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:34,750
♪Dust swirls as I clench my fists♪

224
00:13:34,750 --> 00:13:36,560
♪I strategize, my faith my armor♪

225
00:13:36,560 --> 00:13:38,890
♪My defiance spills onto concrete♪

226
00:13:38,890 --> 00:13:41,320
♪Even thick fog can't hide
my clear gaze♪

227
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:46,370
♪Let neon turn to thorns♪

228
00:13:46,370 --> 00:13:48,260
♪Flying low as the stars shift and turn♪

229
00:13:48,270 --> 00:13:50,210
♪Escape the maze,
transcend the challenge♪

230
00:13:50,210 --> 00:13:52,330
♪The meter starts, breaking the silence♪

231
00:13:52,370 --> 00:13:54,340
♪A beam cuts through
a crack in the wall♪

232
00:13:54,340 --> 00:13:56,510
♪This rhythm and noise
echo through the streets♪

233
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:03,580
♪Don't be afraid. No one will answer♪

234
00:14:03,580 --> 00:14:06,950
♪Why is that child crying?♪

235
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:09,650
♪The shrinking scar on my arm♪

236
00:14:09,650 --> 00:14:11,270
♪Means I've grown up♪

237
00:14:11,270 --> 00:14:14,420
♪You can trust me when I say that♪

238
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:17,900
♪The wound still aches♪

239
00:14:18,310 --> 00:14:22,660
♪Like a biting winter♪

240
00:14:22,660 --> 00:14:25,930
♪But a spark still glows♪

